export default {"id":"djing-level-5","number":5,"title":"Session View as Decks","skillBand":"Textbook","duration":"From the course textbook","summary":"Arrangement View is a fixed timeline. For live and DJ work, order and length of pieces are often not known in advance. Session View is Live’s grid for launching when structure is decided in performance (Manual §7). Songwriting depth belongs","modules":[{"id":"djing-m-5-1","code":"5","title":"Session View as Decks","blurb":"Arrangement View is a fixed timeline. For live and DJ work, order and length of pieces are often not known in advance. Session View is Live’s grid for launching when structure is decided in performance (Manual §7). Songwriting depth belongs","outcomes":[],"sources":[],"practiceFocus":[],"checkpoints":[],"lessons":[{"id":"djing-l-o-5","title":"Section overview","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"overview","blocks":[{"type":"heading","text":"Module 5 — Session View as Decks","level":1},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Objective:</strong> Construct the non-linear DJ instrument and a reusable template.   <strong>Difficulty:</strong> Intermediate build laboratory — one coherent template system.   <strong>Sources:</strong> Live 12 Manual <em>7. Session View</em>; <em>How-to-DJ</em> §4; <em>Foundations of Digital DJing</em> (Session paradigm); <em>DJing Architecture</em>."}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"djing-l-5-1-1","title":"5.1.1 — Session Model and Beginner DJ Template","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"Session versus Arrangement (Manual)","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Arrangement View is a fixed timeline. For live and DJ work, order and length of pieces are often not known in advance. Session View is Live’s grid for launching when structure is decided in performance (Manual §7)."},{"type":"table","headers":["View","Use in this course"],"rows":[["<strong>Session</strong>","Live launching, blending, performance"],["<strong>Arrangement</strong>","Record the set; edit; critique later"]],"caption":null},{"type":"prose","html":"Songwriting depth belongs to the sister course Foundations of Music Production."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Object model","blocks":[{"type":"table","headers":["Object","DJ meaning"],"rows":[["<strong>Track (column)</strong>","One deck or layer; only one clip plays per track at a time"],["<strong>Clip</strong>","Playable object (full song, loop, one-shot)"],["<strong>Scene (row)</strong>","Horizontal moment — launch several clips together"],["<strong>Global quantize</strong>","Delays launches to the next musical boundary (often 1 bar) — enabled for early reliability"],["<strong>Group tracks</strong>","Optional submix containers (Manual); not required for the minimum template"]],"caption":null}]},{"type":"step","title":"Minimum viable template","blocks":[{"type":"table","headers":["Track or element","Configuration"],"rows":[["Deck A / Deck B","Audio tracks; EQ Three and Utility first"],["Deck C (optional)","Third layer or acapella — used sparingly"],["One-shots / FX","Impacts and risers — limited use"],["Return A / B","Shared reverb and delay; high-pass on reverb returns is developed in transition levels"],["Main","Main Out and Cue Out already correct from Module 4"],["Crossfader","Show X; Deck A→A, Deck B→B for classic blends; also practice channel-fader-only mixing with crossfader centered"]],"caption":null},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Naming:</strong> <code>Artist - Title | BPM | CueNote</code>   <strong>Color:</strong> Consistent code for energy, role, or genre, with a written legend. Arbitrary color assignment reduces retrieval under pressure.   <strong>Save as:</strong> <code>DJ Template - Foundations</code>. Cold-open every practice session; confirm Main ≠ Cue, names, and devices."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Procedure — build and stress the template (60–90 minutes)","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Empty Set → create the structure above.  ","Confirm Cue mode remains valid.  ","Import 10 owned full tracks into Deck A/B slots with naming and color.  ","Launch pairs with quantize on; practice wrong-clip recovery: stop on next boundary, then relaunch the correct clip.  ","Scene-launch one prepared transition row after single-clip launches are reliable.  ","Save template; quit; reopen; verify configuration stability."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Common errors","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Building a production Set and treating it as a DJ template  ","Many returns without usage discipline  ","No naming convention under time pressure  ","Quantize off before recovery skills exist  ","Too many simultaneous full Complex Pro layers without a stop habit  "],"ordered":false}]},{"type":"step","title":"Laboratory 5.1.1","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Deliver the saved template, a 10-track Session, and a short recording or notes showing dual launch, wrong-clip recovery, and Main ≠ Cue still intact."},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Pass criteria:</strong> Template reopens cold with two decks ready, devices present, cue path intact; launch and recovery possible without extended browser search."}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"djing-l-5-2-1","title":"5.2.1 — Import Discipline, Launch Control, CPU Awareness","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"5.2.1 — Import Discipline, Launch Control, CPU Awareness","blocks":[{"type":"heading","text":"Stable import paths","level":3},{"type":"prose","html":"Use a dedicated DJ music folder that Live can always locate. Files left in temporary download locations break Sets when moved. Collect and manage files before show day (deep Collect All procedures belong to the sister Ableton course)."},{"type":"heading","text":"Full-track spine versus loops","level":3},{"type":"prose","html":"Early sets: full tracks form the spine. Loops are beds or tools under a deck. Hybrid layer work waits until Module 13."},{"type":"heading","text":"Launch discipline","level":3},{"type":"list","items":["Quantize on for reliability; press slightly early; do not fight the quantize grid with repeated launches.  ","Stopping cleanly is required: abandoned layers produce mix failures.  ","Scene launch for prepared moments after single-clip competence.  ","CPU: stop unused clips; reduce layers; raise buffer (Module 4) if the machine cannot sustain Complex/Pro load."],"ordered":false},{"type":"heading","text":"Laboratory 5.2.1 (performance)","level":3},{"type":"list","items":["From cold template: 20 consecutive clip launches without wrong-deck accidents.  ","Five intentional wrong launches with recoveries logged.  ","Ten-minute continuous dual-deck presence (control confidence; full musical perfection not required)."],"ordered":true},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Pass criteria:</strong> Launch and stop operations automatic; recovery time under one phrase; CPU plan documented for the machine in use."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Module 5 pass","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["[ ] DJ Template - Foundations exists and cold-opens cleanly  ","[ ] Two full tracks launch cleanly with quantize on  ","[ ] Recovery path proven  "],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8}],"exercises":[]}]};
